{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 134, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding the input-to-output residual helps most when no direct 0->3 path exists (#11, #15 large gains)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without a 0->3 shortcut, cutting edge 0 starves node 1 and the deep paths, so the network degrades more (#92 vs #91, #100)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Removing a parameter-free pooling op on the final edge discards little and can remove a harmful smoothing path (#3)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 4 is empty, edge 5 is one of only two inputs to the output, so removing it is far more damaging (#8 vs #4)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 5 absent, edge 4 carries the main conv path into the output, so deleting it leaves only edge 3 (#87)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a 3x3 conv to an empty final edge restores a deep path, a much bigger gain than swapping one op for another (#80, #74)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a pooling op on the first edge with a conv gives node 1 learnable features that feed several downstream edges (#23, #27)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Converting an identity 0->2 edge into a 3x3 conv adds capacity on a path the cell already uses (#31, #36, #38)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Swapping an existing 3x3 conv on 1->2 for an identity removes depth and capacity (#51, #52, #54, #58)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting a parameterised 0->3 connection removes both a shortcut and capacity, which costs much more than deleting other ops there (#64, #67, #70)."}], "tok": 34997, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "none"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "none"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_1x1"], [5, "none"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "none"]], [["none", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "none"]], [["skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "none"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [5, "none"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1"], [5, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["none", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "none", 